          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Given an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endomorphism"} endomorphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon A\to A
            in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/traced+monoidal+category"} traced monoidal category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi.mathscript 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathscr{C}
            there is a natural notion of its
            %em trace
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} tr
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tr(f) \colon 1\to 1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            denotes the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+unit"} tensor unit
          %p
            When
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi.mathscript 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathscr{C}
            is a
            = succeed "-linear" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℂ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fusion+category"} fusion category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} tr
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tr(f)
            with a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+number"} complex number
          %p
            That is, the trace of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            is the unique
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scalar"} scalar
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi λ
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi End
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda \in End(1)
            such that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} tr
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi λ
                  %mo ⋅
                  %msub
                    %mtext id
                    %mn 1
                  %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                    %mrow
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\tr(f)
                  \\,=\,
                  \\lambda
                  \\cdot
                  \\text{id}_1
                  \\mathrlap{\,.}
          %p
            In the case that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+map"} linear
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endomorphism"} endomorphism
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+number"} finite
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimensional vector space
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+algebra"} linear algebra
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            The idea of the trace operation is easily seen in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+diagram"} string diagram
            notation: essentially one takes an endomorphism
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: A\xrightarrow{}A
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mn 1
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mrow
                              %mi tr
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi f
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mn 1
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mn 1
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi a
                            %mo *
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⊗
                        %mtd
                          %mi a
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi Id
                                  %mrow
                                    %msup
                                      %mi a
                                      %mo *
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mi f
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi a
                            %mo *
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⊗
                        %mtd
                          %mi a
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi b
                                  %mrow
                                    %msup
                                      %mi a
                                      %mo *
                                    %mo ,
                                    %mi a
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi a
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⊗
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi a
                            %mo *
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  1
                  \\\
                  \\;\;\;\downarrow^{tr(f)}
                  \\\
                  1
                  }
                  \\;\;\;
                  \:=
                  \\;\;\;
                  \\array{
                  \&amp; 1
                  \\\
                  \&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  a^* &amp;\otimes&amp; a
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{Id_{a^*}}} &amp;&amp; \;\;\downarrow^f
                  \\\
                  a^* &amp;\otimes&amp; a
                  \\\
                  \&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{b_{a^*, a}}}
                  \\\
                  a &amp;\otimes&amp; a^*
                  \\\
                  \&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  \&amp; 1
                  }
          %p
            This definition makes sense in any
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/braided+monoidal+category"} braided monoidal category
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/balanced+monoidal+category"} balancing
          %p
            The trace of the identity
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mn 1
                    %mi a
                  %mo :
                  %mi a
                  %mo →
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1_a:a \to a
            is called the
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euler+characteristic"} Euler characteristic
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vect"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi Vect
                          %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C = Vect_k
                with its standard monoidal structure (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+vector+spaces"}> tensor product of vector spaces
                ): in this case
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi tr
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} tr(f)
                is the usual trace of a linear map. Indeed, suppose
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                is an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endomorphism"} endomorphism
                on a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+dimensional+vector+space"}
                  finite dimensional
                  = succeed "-vector" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi k
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi V
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi tr
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi k
                      %mo →
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} tr(f) \colon k\to k
                is given by the following composition.
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mi η
                      %mi V
                      %mo ⊗
                      %msup
                        %mi V
                        %mo *
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                          %mi f
                          %mo ⊗
                          %mi id
                      %mi V
                      %mo ⊗
                      %msup
                        %mi V
                        %mo *
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mi ε
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k\xrightarrow{\eta} V\otimes V^\ast\xrightarrow{f\otimes id}V\otimes V^\ast\xrightarrow{\varepsilon} k
              %p
                Here
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ε
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varepsilon
                is the standard
                = succeed "-pairing." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/evaluation"} evaluation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi η
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta
                is obtained from the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dual+linear+map"} dual linear map
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ε
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varepsilon
                by applying the following isomorphisms, see (
                %a{:href => "#DoldPuppe1978"}> Dold &amp; Puppe 1978
                ).
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo ≅
                      %msup
                        %mi k
                        %mo *
                      %mo ,
                      %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi V
                      %mo ⊗
                      %msup
                        %mi V
                        %mo *
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo *
                      %mo ≅
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi V
                        %mo *
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo *
                      %mo ⊗
                      %msup
                        %mi V
                        %mo *
                      %mo ≅
                      %mi V
                      %mo ⊗
                      %msup
                        %mi V
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k\cong k^\ast,\qquad (V\otimes V^\ast)^\ast\cong(V^\ast)^\ast\otimes V^\ast\cong V\otimes V^\ast
              %p One can then compute that
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi η
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi λ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %munderover
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo =
                          %mn 1
                        %mi n
                      %mi λ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi e
                        %mi i
                      %mo ⊗
                      %msubsup
                        %mi e
                        %mi i
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta(\lambda)=\sum_{i=1}^n\lambda (e_i\otimes e_i^\ast),
              %p
                where
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi e
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi …
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi e
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{e_1,\ldots,e_n\}
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+basis"} linear basis
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msubsup
                        %mi e
                        %mn 1
                        %mo *
                      %mo ,
                      %mi …
                      %mo ,
                      %msubsup
                        %mi e
                        %mi n
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{e_1^\ast,\ldots,e_n^\ast\}
                is the
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "dual+vector+space#dual_bases"} dual basis
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                is given in this basis by a matrix
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi a
                          %mi ij
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a_ij)
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi id
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi η
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi λ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi λ
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %mrow
                          %mtable{:displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %msub
                                  %mi a
                                  %mrow
                                    %mn 1
                                    %mi i
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mi ⋮
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %msub
                                  %mi a
                                  %mi ni
                        %mo )
                      %mo ⊗
                      %msubsup
                        %mi e
                        %mi i
                        %mo *
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f\otimes id)(\eta(\lambda))=\lambda\sum\begin{pmatrix}a_{1i}\\\vdots\\a_{ni}\end{pmatrix}\otimes e_i^\ast.
              %p
                Finally,
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi tr
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi λ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (tr(f))(\lambda)
                is obtained by applying the pairing on this tensor:
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi tr
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi λ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mi λ
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                        %msub
                          %mi a
                          %mi ii
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (tr(f))(\lambda)=\lambda\sum a_{ii}
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo =
                      %mi SuperVect
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi Vect
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi ℤ
                            %mn 2
                      %mo ,
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C = SuperVect = (Vect_{\mathbb{Z}_2}, \otimes, b)
                , the category of
                = succeed "-graded" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}_2
                = succeed "trivial" do
                  %em non
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} -1
                on two odd graded vector spaces: in this case the above is the
                %strong
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supertrace"} supertrace
                on supervectorspaces,
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi str
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi V
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mi tr
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi V
                          %mi even
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo −
                        %mi tr
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi V
                          %mi odd
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} str(V) = tr(V_{even}) - tr(V_odd)
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo =
                      %mi Span
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi Top
                        %mi op
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C = Span(Top^{op})
                \: here the trace is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/co-span+co-trace"} co-span co-trace
                which can be seen as describing the gluing of in/out boundaries of
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism"} cobordisms
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo =
                      %mi Span
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Grpd
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C = Span(Grpd)
                \: this reproduces the notion of trace of a linear map within the interpretation of spans of groupoids as linear maps in the context of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoidification"} groupoidification
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+function+theory"} geometric function theory
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/span+trace"} span trace
            %li
              %p
                In the
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+%28infinity%2C1%29-category+of+spectra"} symmetric monoidal (infinity,1)-category of spectra
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/suspension+spectrum"} suspension spectrum
                of a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euler+characteristic"} Euler characteristic
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                (see there).
          %h2#generalizations Generalizations
          %h3#vertical_categorification Vertical categorification
          %p
            See
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trace+of+a+category"} trace of a category
          %h3#horizontal_categorification Horizontal categorification
          %p
            See
            = succeed "." do
              %span.newWikiWord
                trace in a bicategory
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/trace+in+a+bicategory"} ?
          %h3#partial_trace Partial trace
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V \in C
            be a dualizable object, and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            any object. From an endomorphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V \otimes W
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi tr
                    %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} tr_V(f)
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
          .query
            %p TO DO: Draw the diagram just described.
          %h4#matrix_representation Matrix representation
          %p
            Suppose
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            are finite-dimensional vector spaces over a field, with dimensions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi m
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L(A)
            denote the space of linear operators on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %strong partial trace
            over
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo
                      %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} _{W}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi L
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↦
                  %msub
                    %mi Tr
                    %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi L
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  T \in L(V \otimes W) \mapsto Tr_{W}(T) \in L(V).
          .un_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mi m
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e_{1}, \ldots, e_{m}
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_{1}, \ldots, f_{n}
              be bases for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              respectively. Then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              has a matrix representation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mi l
                        %mo ,
                        %mi i
                        %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{a_{k l,i j}\}
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi k
                    %mo ,
                    %mi i
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi m
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 \le k,i \le m
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi l
                    %mo ,
                    %mi j
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 \le l,j \le n
              relative to the basis of the space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V \otimes W
              given by
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi e
                        %mi k
                      %mo ⊗
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mi l
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e_{k} \otimes f_{l}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo ,
                        %mi i
                    %mo =
                    %munderover
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi j
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %mi n
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mi j
                        %mo ,
                        %mi i
                        %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    b_{k,i} = \sum_{j=1}^{n}a_{k j,i j}
            %p
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo ,
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k,i
              over
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi …
                      %mo ,
                      %mi m
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1, \ldots, m
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi b
                        %mrow
                          %mi k
                          %mo ,
                          %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b_{k,i}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              is independent of the choice of bases and is defined as the partial trace.
          %h4#example Example
          %p
            Consider a quantum system,
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ρ
                      %mi env
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho_{env}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+information+theory"} quantum information theory
            as the CNOT gate:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo =
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mn 00
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mn 00
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo +
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mn 01
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mn 01
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo +
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mn 11
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mn 10
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo +
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mn 10
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mn 11
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  U={|00\rangle}{\langle 00|} + {|01\rangle}{\langle 01|} + {|11\rangle}{\langle 10|} + {|10\rangle}{\langle 11|}.
          %p
            Suppose our system has the simple state
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {|1\rangle}{\langle 1|}
            and the environment has the simple state
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                      %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {|0\rangle}{\langle 0|}
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msub
                      %mi ρ
                      %mi env
                    %mo =
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mn 10
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                      %mn 10
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho \otimes \rho_{env} = {|10\rangle}{\langle 10|}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mfrac
                    %mn 1
                    %mn 2
                  %msub
                    %mi Tr
                    %mi env
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo ⊗
                  %msub
                    %mi ρ
                    %mi env
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msup
                    %mi U
                    %mo †
                  %mo =
                  %mfrac
                    %mn 1
                    %mn 2
                  %msub
                    %mi Tr
                    %mi env
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mn 10
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mn 10
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo +
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mn 11
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mn 11
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                        %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                      %mo +
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %mn 2
                  %mo =
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  T(\rho) = \frac{1}{2}Tr_{env}U(\rho \otimes \rho_{env})U^{\dagger}
                  \= \frac{1}{2}Tr_{env}({|10\rangle}{\langle 10|} + {|11\rangle}{\langle 11|})
                  \= \frac{{|1\rangle}{\langle 1|}{\langle 0|0\rangle} + {|1\rangle}{\langle 1|}{\langle 1|1\rangle}}{2}
                  \= {|1\rangle}{\langle 1|}
          %p
            where we inserted the normalization factor
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{1}{2}
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relation+between+trace+and+determinant"} relation between trace and determinant
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/traced+monoidal+category"} traced monoidal category
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euler+characteristic"} Euler characteristic
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bicategorical+trace"}> bicategorical trace
                ,
              %ul
                %li
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Reidemeister+trace"} Reidemeister trace
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+trace"} higher trace
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dennis+trace"}> Dennis trace
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cyclotomic+trace"} cyclotomic trace
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trace+of+horizontal+to+round+chord+diagrams"} trace of horizontal to round chord diagrams
          %h2#references References
          %p The categorical notion of trace in a monoidal category is due to
          %ul
            %li#DoldPuppe1978
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Albrecht+Dold"}> Albrecht Dold
              , and
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dieter+Puppe"} Dieter Puppe
              %em Duality, trace, and transfer
              In Proceedings of the Inter-
              %p national Conference on Geometric Topology (Warsaw, 1978), pages 81{102, Warsaw, 1980. PWN.
          %p and
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Max+Kelly"} Max Kelly
              M. L. Laplaza,
              %em Coherence for compact closed categories
              J. Pure Appl. Algebra, 19:193{213, 1980.
          %p Surveys include
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Selinger"}> Peter Selinger
                ,
                %em A survey of graphical languages for monoidal categories
                (
                %a{:href => "http://www.mathstat.dal.ca/~selinger/papers/graphical.pdf"}> pdf
                ), Section 5
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kate+Ponto"}> Kate Ponto
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Shulman"} Mike Shulman
                %em Traces in symmetric monoidal categories
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/pdf/1107.6032v1.pdf"}> pdf
                ).
          %p
            Generalization of this to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/indexed+monoidal+categories"} indexed monoidal categories
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kate+Ponto"}> Kate Ponto
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Shulman"} Mike Shulman
              = succeed "," do
                %em Duality and traces for indexed monoidal categories
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1211.1555"} arXiv:1211.1555
          %p
            and to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bicategories"} bicategories
            in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kate+Ponto"}> Kate Ponto
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Shulman"} Mike Shulman
              = succeed "," do
                %em Shadows and traces in bicategories
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0910.1306"} arXiv:0910.1306
          %p Further developments are in
          %ul#BenZviNadler13
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andre+Joyal"}> Andre Joyal
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ross+Street"} Ross Street
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dominic+Verity"} Dominic Verity
                %em Traced Monoidal Categories
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Ben-Zvi"}> David Ben-Zvi
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Nadler"} David Nadler
                %em Nonlinear traces
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1305.7175"}> arXiv:1305.7175
                )
          %p
            For the notion of partial trace, particularly its application to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+mechanics"} quantum mechanics
          %ul
            %li
              Nielsen and Chuang,
              %em Quantum Computation and Quantum Information
